### Key finding

The attractiveness function (weighted sum of length + depth + recency + mvp_count) produces **measurably different rankings** across weight configs:
- **diff_rate = 0.52** (21/40 weight pairs produce different top-1 chains) — well above random baseline (~0.17)
- **min score spread = 1.0** — non-trivial chain discrimination confirmed
- All-zero weights → 0.0 (R6.3 verified)
- Equal weights → identical rankings (idempotence verified)

